    <!--
    Complete geometric and kinematic description of the AgileX Ranger Air base.

    Macro parameters:
      name              Prefix used for the optional joint to the parent model.
      parent_link       Link to which the base is attached in a stationary setup.
      xyz / rpy         Pose of the base relative to parent_link.
      use_mock_hardware Compatibility parameter passed by the calling description;
                        no hardware interface is created in this file.
      attach_to_parent  If true, creates a fixed joint to parent_link. If false,
                        ranger_base_link remains the movable root link in Gazebo.
      fix_wheel_joints  If true, steering and wheel joints are fixed. If false,
                        they are continuous joints and can rotate.

    For most links, the sections have the following meaning:
      inertial  Physical mass, centre of mass and inertia tensor for simulation.
      visual    Mesh and material shown in RViz/Gazebo.
      collision Geometry used by the physics engine and collision checking.
    -->
